    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0698" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg574"/>

                <head>No. 346.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Sir Edward
                        Thornton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 17,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 23d ultimo, with its several inclosures, in relation to an
                    attack alleged to have been made by a number of Gros Ventres and Mandin Indians
                    from the United States upon a party of Stony Indians of Canada, during which
                    about eight of the latter were killed and several more wounded.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to inform you that I have communicated a copy of your note to my
                    colleague, the Secretary of the Interior, in order that the facts may be
                    inquired into, with a view to such action by this government as may be found to
                    be proper.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
